solution_str:
$$19x + 1 - 4x - 81 =$$ Start by combining all like terms
\begin{align}
19x - 4x &= 15x \tag{Like Terms } 
\\\\ 1 - 81& = -80\tag{Like Terms }
\end{align}
Simplify
Starting with the given 
19x + 1 - 4x - 81
We first combine like terms  
19x - 4x = 15x
1 - 8 = -80
Rearranged order  
15x - 80

The simplified expression is \boxed{15x-80}

